Description: ParaView in Sparky Stereo OS offers one stereo output, the declared pair
 The render views start as a stereo pair handed to the desktop (Crystal Eyes: a
 quad-buffered window, which the edition's Mesa packs side by side and declares
 to Stereo KWin), and the desktop makes each screen's format. "Enable 3D", a
 Render View setting on by default, decides it at ParaView's start (ParaView's
 own "restart required" notice says so); the View menu has "Enable 3D" and
 "3D display settings..." (KScreen).
 .
 ParaView's own stereo output formats (Red-Blue, Interlaced, Dresden, Anaglyph,
 Checkerboard, SplitViewportHorizontal) are not offered: --stereo-type takes
 'Crystal Eyes' only and refuses the others with a sentence that says what to
 use instead; the Render View's StereoType and ServerStereoType keep Crystal
 Eyes, Left, Right and None and are not shown in the properties panel; the
 screenshot's stereo modes keep No change, No stereo, Left Eye Only, Right Eye
 Only and Both Eyes. A state file or a saved setting that names one of the six
 opens in the stereo pair (or flat with Enable 3D off) and the person is told
 once; a saved screenshot mode among them saves the picture as shown, with a
 warning. VTK's vtkRenderWindow keeps every stereo type for the other programs
 that load it. When the desktop gives the view no stereo pair, the person is
 told once that the views are flat.
 .
 Every input, reader, filter, CAVE and remote rendering function stays. The
 sentences are in the gettext domain paraview-stereo (Clients/ParaView/
 stereo-po, from the edition's translations patch).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
